          "id": "e0f15c7796e9773431ef47df046336fd8b2b5735",
          "message": "update the required version of lm-eval package to the latest. (#100)\n\nWe've been using a commit id to specify a particular version of the\r\nlm-eval harness tool. that particular commit has been merged into the\r\nv0.4.4 release. We should be using that release going forward. [another\r\nreason is a deprecation message we're getting for using the egg\r\nfragment: `DEPRECATION:\r\ngit+https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness.git@a4987bba6e9e9b3f22bd3a6c1ecf0abd04fd5622#egg=lm_eval[api]\r\ncontains an egg fragment with a non-PEP 508 name pip 25.0 will enforce\r\nthis behaviour change. A possible replacement is to use the req @ url\r\nsyntax, and remove the egg fragment. Discussion can be found at\r\nhttps://github.com/pypa/pip/issues/11617`\r\n]\r\n\r\nTEST PLAN\r\nthe remote push run for my commit\r\n[completed](https://github.com/neuralmagic/nm-vllm-ent/actions/runs/11243292573)\r\nwith just a test_scheduler failure that's consistent with other jobs and\r\nindependent of this change. a [nightly\r\nrun](https://github.com/neuralmagic/nm-vllm-ent/actions/runs/11254332924)\r\nis queued.\r\nnote that the LM-EVAL jobs as part of these runs are not affected by\r\nthis change because those are using the HuggingFace fork of the lm-eval\r\nharness from EtheriumAI.",
